{{smaller block|On, ''bacons'', on!
{{right|''Shak.'', 1 Hen. IV., ii. 2.}}}}
'''To save one’s bacon,''' {{smaller|to preserve one’s self from harm.}}
{{smaller block|<poem>But here I say the Turks were much mistaken,
Who, hating hogs, yet wished ''to save their bacon.''</poem>
{{right|''Byron'', Don Juan, vii. 42.}}}}

'''bacon-beetle''' (bā′kọn-bē″tl), ''n.'' A species of the genus ''Dermestes'', ''D. lardarius'', family ''Dermestidæ'', order ''Coleoptera'', whose larvæ are very destructive to stuffed animals in museums. The larvæ are hairy, and whitish-brown in color.
