'''Baconian''' (bạ̄-kō′ni-an), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< Francis ''Bacon'', born 1561, died 1626.] '''I.''' ''a.'' Pertaining to Francis Bacon, Baron Verulam, commonly called Lord Bacon: as, the ''Baconian'' philosophy.—'''Baconian method''', {{smaller|a term often, though incorrectly, applied to the method of}}
